  "id": "COMPOUND:3095 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin appears to interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect pathways, all of which involve the enzyme UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. The first pathway links Isoliquiritigenin to the electron transfer flavoprotein-ubiquinone oxidoreductase, mitochondrial, which is targeted by 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin, a compound that in turn targets CDC2L1. The second and third pathways demonstrate that Isoliquiritigenin directly or indirectly targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which is a known target of Acetamide and Sennoside D, both of which also target CDC2L1. These findings suggest that Isoliquiritigenin may exert its effects on CDC2L1 through the modulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, potentially by inhibiting its activity or altering its substrate specificity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Isoliquiritigenin and CDC2L1, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, emphasizing the need for further experimental validation to confirm the direct or indirect role of Isoliquiritigenin in regulating CDC2L1 activity.",
